8,"height":128,"uv_width":128,"uv_height":128,"particle":false,"use_as_default":true,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","file_format":"png","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","wrap_mode":"limited","pbr_channel":"color","fps":7,"frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"fc9cec02-ac77-5955-847c-a78a602b1b82","source":"data:image/png;base64,","relative_path":""}],"description":"# wall_corner_softwood_cracked\n\nDamaged state below 70 % HP of `wall_corner_softwood` (Patch 5): the same wooden (softwood) piece with dark cracks, a few tips or merlons knocked off and splinters or chips. The game swaps it in below 70 % HP and back above 70 % when repaired.\n\nSoftwood wall corner: an L joint filling one column; walls leave along -X... +X (north face) and along +Z (west face), with a corner post.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y 0..119, z -8..8 units.\n- Texture: 128 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: 10, all in `finished`; the construction and ruined state sets and the damaged/abandoned texture variants were removed in Patch 5 (the game draws none of them for buildings).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 106 x 16 centred at the origin"}